Article 3 A circuit court shall adjudicate or handle the following cases within the circuit area that shall be accepted by the Supreme People's Court:
(1) First-instance administrative cases of major and complex nature nationwide;
(2) First-instance civil and commercial cases with significant impact nationwide;
(3) Cases appealed against first-instance administrative or civil and commercial judgments or rulings made by a Higher People's Court;
(4) Cases applying for retrial against effective administrative or civil and commercial judgments, rulings, or mediation statements made by a Higher People's Court;
(5) Criminal petition cases;
(6) Cases initiating retrial ex officio according to law;
(7) Cases applying for reconsideration against decisions on fines or detention made by a Higher People's Court;
(8) Cases submitted by a Higher People's Court to the Supreme People's Court for a ruling or decision on jurisdictional issues;
(9) Cases submitted by a Higher People's Court for approval of extending the trial period;
(10) Civil and commercial cases involving Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, and judicial assistance cases;
(11) Other cases which the Supreme People's Court deems shall be adjudicated or handled by a circuit court.
A circuit court shall, according to law, handle matters of letters and visits submitted to the Supreme People's Court within the circuit area.
